    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-28b-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28B(6) Unfair trading practices towards consumers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-28b-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(6) Without limiting subsection (2), the following are examples of\nconduct that may be unfair trading practices:\n\n(a) impeding the consumer’s ability to exercise legal rights, or\nseek legal remedies;\n\n(b) failing to disclose material information to the consumer;\n\n(c) disclosing material information to the consumer in a\ncomplex, ineffective, unclear, unintelligible, ambiguous,\nuntimely or overwhelming way;\n\n(d) creating an environment (including by using design elements\nin digital interfaces) which places the consumer under\nunreasonable pressure in relation to, or obstructs the\nconsumer from, making or fulfilling the consumer’s decision.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) Without limiting subsection (2), the following are examples of\nconduct that may be unfair trading practices:\n\n(a) impeding the consumer’s ability to exercise legal rights, or\nseek legal remedies;\n\n(b) failing to disclose material information to the consumer;\n\n(c) disclosing material information to the consumer in a\ncomplex, ineffective, unclear, unintelligible, ambiguous,\nuntimely or overwhelming way;\n\n(d) creating an environment (including by using design elements\nin digital interfaces) which places the consumer under\nunreasonable pressure in relation to, or obstructs the\nconsumer from, making or fulfilling the consumer’s decision.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-28b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-28b-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-28b-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5d71c907d6015c7366571f0c4c42e5f8f6c6a8f60849f5196a98af002fd17805",
      "skos:note": "Examples of conduct that may be unfair trading practices towards consumers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-28b-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28B(6) Unfair trading practices towards consumers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(6) Without limiting subsection (2), the following are examples of\nconduct that may be unfair trading practices:\n\n(a) impeding the consumer’s ability to exercise legal rights, or\nseek legal remedies;\n\n(b) failing to disclose material information to the consumer;\n\n(c) disclosing material information to the consumer in a\ncomplex, ineffective, unclear, unintelligible, ambiguous,\nuntimely or overwhelming way;\n\n(d) creating an environment (including by using design elements\nin digital interfaces) which places the consumer under\nunreasonable pressure in relation to, or obstructs the\nconsumer from, making or fulfilling the consumer’s decision."
    },
