    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48A Transaction based charges to be displayed in certain",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-48a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "circumstances\nRequirement to display\n\n(1) This section applies in relation to goods or services of a kind\nordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or\nconsumption.\n\n(2) A person who, in trade or commerce, in offering to supply goods or\nservices to another person, displays a base price for any of the\ngoods or services must display in accordance with subsection (3)\nthe following information for any transaction based charge for the\nsupply:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) if the amount of the transaction based charge can be\ncalculated—the amount of the transaction based charge;\nor\n\n(ii) in any other case—the method for calculating the\ntransaction based charge;\n\n(b) that it is a per transaction charge;\n\n(c) whether the transaction based charge is or may be payable;\n\n(d) whether or not the base price displayed includes the\ntransaction based charge.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "circumstances\nRequirement to display\n\n(1) This section applies in relation to goods or services of a kind\nordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or\nconsumption.\n\n(2) A person who, in trade or commerce, in offering to supply goods or\nservices to another person, displays a base price for any of the\ngoods or services must display in accordance with subsection (3)\nthe following information for any transaction based charge for the\nsupply:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) if the amount of the transaction based charge can be\ncalculated—the amount of the transaction based charge;\nor\n\n(ii) in any other case—the method for calculating the\ntransaction based charge;\n\n(b) that it is a per transaction charge;\n\n(c) whether the transaction based charge is or may be payable;\n\n(d) whether or not the base price displayed includes the\ntransaction based charge.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c3885686ca74917edbc8f8c8a9d2430f3c70637cc90a0af380a250760feedd33"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-48a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48A Transaction based charges to be displayed in certain",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "circumstances\nRequirement to display\n\n(1) This section applies in relation to goods or services of a kind\nordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or\nconsumption.\n\n(2) A person who, in trade or commerce, in offering to supply goods or\nservices to another person, displays a base price for any of the\ngoods or services must display in accordance with subsection (3)\nthe following information for any transaction based charge for the\nsupply:\n\n(a) either:\n\n(i) if the amount of the transaction based charge can be\ncalculated—the amount of the transaction based charge;\nor\n\n(ii) in any other case—the method for calculating the\ntransaction based charge;\n\n(b) that it is a per transaction charge;\n\n(c) whether the transaction based charge is or may be payable;\n\n(d) whether or not the base price displayed includes the\ntransaction based charge.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
