      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the requirement is that the\ncontract contains terms that have the effect of providing:\n\n(a) for supply of goods or services in, or recurring or continuing\nsupply of goods or services for, a fixed period; and\n\n(b) for supply, or continuing supply, of goods or services to\ncontinue after the end of the fixed period unless a party to the\ncontract stops the supply or continuing supply or the contract\nis terminated; and\n\n(c) for a person to automatically incur liability to pay for the\nsupplies or continuing supply; and\n\n(d) a right for that person to end the contract.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the requirement is that the\ncontract contains terms that have the effect of providing:\n\n(a) for supply of goods or services in, or recurring or continuing\nsupply of goods or services for, a fixed period; and\n\n(b) for supply, or continuing supply, of goods or services to\ncontinue after the end of the fixed period unless a party to the\ncontract stops the supply or continuing supply or the contract\nis terminated; and\n\n(c) for a person to automatically incur liability to pay for the\nsupplies or continuing supply; and\n\n(d) a right for that person to end the contract.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48b-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2f312b1010ce89f61ac79878279097cbd089a9d13c02e39b5808cc6523849deb",
      "skos:note": "Contract terms must provide for automatic liability and termination rights.",
      "dc:description": "(a) supply of goods or services in a fixed period, (b) supply of goods or services to continue after the end of the fixed period, (c) a person to automatically incur liability to pay for supplies or continuing supply, and (d) a right for that person to end the contract."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-48b-ss-3",
