    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48C Excluded subscription contracts",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-48c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following contracts are excluded subscription contracts:\n\n(a) a lease;\n\n(b) a licence in respect of real property;\n\n(c) a contract of hire-purchase;\n\n(d) a contract for payment in instalments;\n\n(e) a contract for supply of childcare;\n\n(f) a contract for supply by a pre-school or school of tuition at a\npre-school, pre-primary, primary or secondary level;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nSubscription contracts  Part 3\n\nNo. 64, 2026\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Unfair Trading Practices) Act\n\n(g) a contract of a kind prescribed for the purposes of this\nparagraph.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901 or paragraph (1)(g) of this section, regulations made for the\npurposes of that paragraph may prescribe the following:\n\n(a) that a kind of contract is a prescribed kind of contract only in\nspecified circumstances;\n\n(b) different circumstances for different kinds of contract.\nSubdivision B—Information requirements",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The following contracts are excluded subscription contracts:\n\n(a) a lease;\n\n(b) a licence in respect of real property;\n\n(c) a contract of hire-purchase;\n\n(d) a contract for payment in instalments;\n\n(e) a contract for supply of childcare;\n\n(f) a contract for supply by a pre-school or school of tuition at a\npre-school, pre-primary, primary or secondary level;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nSubscription contracts  Part 3\n\nNo. 64, 2026\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Unfair Trading Practices) Act\n\n(g) a contract of a kind prescribed for the purposes of this\nparagraph.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901 or paragraph (1)(g) of this section, regulations made for the\npurposes of that paragraph may prescribe the following:\n\n(a) that a kind of contract is a prescribed kind of contract only in\nspecified circumstances;\n\n(b) different circumstances for different kinds of contract.\nSubdivision B—Information requirements",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e58cf838467b4122f07f3710b1a0884d00f226de2b1312e176f1af68c6e58c69"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-48c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48C Excluded subscription contracts",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following contracts are excluded subscription contracts:\n\n(a) a lease;\n\n(b) a licence in respect of real property;\n\n(c) a contract of hire-purchase;\n\n(d) a contract for payment in instalments;\n\n(e) a contract for supply of childcare;\n\n(f) a contract for supply by a pre-school or school of tuition at a\npre-school, pre-primary, primary or secondary level;\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nSubscription contracts  Part 3\n\nNo. 64, 2026\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Unfair Trading Practices) Act\n\n(g) a contract of a kind prescribed for the purposes of this\nparagraph.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901 or paragraph (1)(g) of this section, regulations made for the\npurposes of that paragraph may prescribe the following:\n\n(a) that a kind of contract is a prescribed kind of contract only in\nspecified circumstances;\n\n(b) different circumstances for different kinds of contract.\nSubdivision B—Information requirements"
    },
