    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48g-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48G(3) Meeting the consumer requirement or the small business",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-48g-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf, p.21",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In counting for the purposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(i) the number\nof persons that a person employs:\n\n(a) a casual employee is not to be counted unless employed on a\nregular and systematic basis; and\n\n(b) a part-time employee (including a part-time casual employee\ncounted under paragraph (a) of this subsection) is to be\ncounted as an appropriate fraction of a full-time equivalent.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In counting for the purposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(i) the number\nof persons that a person employs:\n\n(a) a casual employee is not to be counted unless employed on a\nregular and systematic basis; and\n\n(b) a part-time employee (including a part-time casual employee\ncounted under paragraph (a) of this subsection) is to be\ncounted as an appropriate fraction of a full-time equivalent.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48g"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48g-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48g-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "426a3a741d53ac03621b895ffeaffc222dfdb892837282d09c7ac1c9c76cf87c",
      "skos:note": "Employment counting rules for the purposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(i)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-48g-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48G(3) Meeting the consumer requirement or the small business",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 21,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In counting for the purposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(i) the number\nof persons that a person employs:\n\n(a) a casual employee is not to be counted unless employed on a\nregular and systematic basis; and\n\n(b) a part-time employee (including a part-time casual employee\ncounted under paragraph (a) of this subsection) is to be\ncounted as an appropriate fraction of a full-time equivalent.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48g-ss-3-norm",
