    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48h-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48H(3) Standard form contracts for the purposes of this Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-48h-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this Division, a contract may be determined to\nbe a standard form contract despite the existence of one or more of\nthe following:\n\n(a) an opportunity for the subscriber to negotiate changes, to\nterms of the contract, that are minor or insubstantial in effect;\n\n(b) an opportunity for the subscriber to select a term from a\nrange of options determined by the supplier;\n\n(c) an opportunity for a party to another contract or proposed\ncontract to negotiate terms of the other contract or proposed\ncontract.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) For the purposes of this Division, a contract may be determined to\nbe a standard form contract despite the existence of one or more of\nthe following:\n\n(a) an opportunity for the subscriber to negotiate changes, to\nterms of the contract, that are minor or insubstantial in effect;\n\n(b) an opportunity for the subscriber to select a term from a\nrange of options determined by the supplier;\n\n(c) an opportunity for a party to another contract or proposed\ncontract to negotiate terms of the other contract or proposed\ncontract.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48h"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48h-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48h-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bade877a01a5da8ec08fc2aaaf08ed1b29e07bc6870f636faaafe1e1a5230abd",
      "skos:note": "Contract may be a standard form contract despite minor negotiation opportunities."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-48h-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48H(3) Standard form contracts for the purposes of this Division",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this Division, a contract may be determined to\nbe a standard form contract despite the existence of one or more of\nthe following:\n\n(a) an opportunity for the subscriber to negotiate changes, to\nterms of the contract, that are minor or insubstantial in effect;\n\n(b) an opportunity for the subscriber to select a term from a\nrange of options determined by the supplier;\n\n(c) an opportunity for a party to another contract or proposed\ncontract to negotiate terms of the other contract or proposed\ncontract."
    },
