    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Review of operation of amendments made by this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe Commonwealth Minister (within the meaning of Schedule 2 to the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010) must cause a review to be\nconducted of the operation, during the 2 years from the commencement\nof this Part, of the following:\n\n(a) the amendments made by this Part;\n\n(b) any legislative instruments made for the purposes of\nDivision 4A of Part 3-1 of Schedule 2 to the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010.\n(2)\nThe review must be completed, and a written report on the review must\nbe given to the Commonwealth Minister, within 6 months after the end\nof those 2 years.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe Commonwealth Minister (within the meaning of Schedule 2 to the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010) must cause a review to be\nconducted of the operation, during the 2 years from the commencement\nof this Part, of the following:\n\n(a) the amendments made by this Part;\n\n(b) any legislative instruments made for the purposes of\nDivision 4A of Part 3-1 of Schedule 2 to the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010.\n(2)\nThe review must be completed, and a written report on the review must\nbe given to the Commonwealth Minister, within 6 months after the end\nof those 2 years.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-21-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-21-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c8df1405eea43308c9a60709ede652e1ef77aece464013644dcc5b56a7ec8d85",
      "skos:note": "Review of operation of amendments made by this Part"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026#sch-1-sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Review of operation of amendments made by this Part",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe Commonwealth Minister (within the meaning of Schedule 2 to the\nCompetition and Consumer Act 2010) must cause a review to be\nconducted of the operation, during the 2 years from the commencement\nof this Part, of the following:\n\n(a) the amendments made by this Part;\n\n(b) any legislative instruments made for the purposes of\nDivision 4A of Part 3-1 of Schedule 2 to the Competition and\nConsumer Act 2010.\n(2)\nThe review must be completed, and a written report on the review must\nbe given to the Commonwealth Minister, within 6 months after the end\nof those 2 years.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
